1c3d|n|A meeting together of people, at a stated time and place, for the purpose of traffic (as in cattle, provisions, wares, etc.) by private purchase and sale, and not by auction; as, a market is held in the town every week. ; A public place (as an open space in a town) or a large building, where a market is held; a market place or market house; esp., a place where provisions are sold. ; An opportunity for selling anything; demand, as shown by price offered or obtainable; a town, region, or country, where the demand exists; as, to find a market for one's wares; there is no market for woolen cloths in that region; India is a market for English goods. ; Exchange, or purchase and sale; traffic; as, a dull market; a slow market. ; The price for which a thing is sold in a market; market price. Hence: Value; worth. ; The privelege granted to a town of having a public market.	a:8m0,72,7;18gv,59,8;3b2,49,973;1132,39,10;p7p,37,14;dcb,33,12;2m7,31,23;uau,30,15;vw7,30,66;s0u,29,12;8o9,27,10;1h9v,26,6;xtp,24,6;fho,24,8;1em2,22,6~3b2,49,973;vw7,30,66;fj,12,43;isl,11,25;2m7,31,23;1ptt,19,22;1it4,5,18;1iii,11,16;1ipe,13,16;uau,30,15;p7p,37,14;dcb,33,12;s0u,29,12;1ejx,14,11;8o9,27,10	v:1q8u,34,4;b50,8,10;1h9v,0,1~b50,8,10;1q8u,34,4;1h9v,0,1	V:1itl,36,7;2am5,32,2;b50,28,41;17un,23,7;15gp,21,26;2dn0,21,10;y6k,18,6;280r,16,4;20pj,15,14;2h5,11,8;1ano,6,9;1a7t,6,2;1vj4,5,7;1rsy,4,3;2dwy,4,6~b50,28,41;15gp,21,26;20pj,15,14;2dn0,21,10;1ano,6,9;2h5,11,8;1vj4,5,7;17un,23,7;1itl,36,7;y6k,18,6;2dwy,4,6;280r,16,4;1rsy,4,3;1a7t,6,2;2am5,32,2	n:18gv,70,17;ard,70,3;17cm,64,1342;18gj,64,34;4cg,58,6;8m0,54,2;1gx9,49,10;11q1,49,7;gil,49,5;24m6,41,83;1c9g,40,13;2q7,40,12;1ojm,29,77;q26,27,9;1llc,26,10~17cm,64,1342;3b2,15,93;24m6,41,83;1ojm,29,77;y87,18,76;4bp,14,74;18gj,64,34;2g08,24,24;18gv,70,17;1c9g,40,13;2q7,40,12;2esi,6,11;1gx9,49,10;1llc,26,10;q26,27,9	N:q4i,99,36;1ma1,84,7;l6i,76,7;2dmz,65,7;10cu,59,7;va7,55,20;p09,54,7;2am5,52,8;15gu,49,6;2a4t,46,4;1scf,45,3;1spn,41,6;198z,39,6;4bp,36,342;o